---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const aboutSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'AboutPage',
	name: 'About League of Legendary Women',
	url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site),
	description: 'Learn about the mission, sources, editorial approach, and privacy practices behind League of Legendary Women.',
};
---
<BaseLayout
	title="About League of Legendary Women"
	description="Learn about the mission, sources, editorial approach, and privacy practices behind League of Legendary Women."
	structuredData={aboutSchema}
>
	<article class="text-page">
		<p class="eyebrow">About the archive</p>
		<h1>History belongs to everyone.</h1>
		<p class="lead">League of Legendary Women is a growing collection celebrating women whose ideas, courage, and work shaped the world.</p>
		<h2>Inspired by Emily</h2>
		<p>This project was inspired by my daughter, Emily, and the hope that she will always have powerful examples of women who imagined boldly, persevered courageously, and changed the world.</p>
		<h2>How the catalog works</h2>
		<p>Every profile is stored as structured data in the GitHub repository. Updates are reviewed, built into a static site, and published without a database or user accounts.</p>
		<h2>Install League of Legendary Women</h2>
		<p>You can install this website on your device for quick access and an app-like experience.</p>
		<div class="install-instructions">
			<section>
				<h3>Windows</h3>
				<ol>
					<li>Open the site in Microsoft Edge or Google Chrome.</li>
					<li>Select the install icon in the address bar, or open the browser menu and choose <strong>Install League of Legendary Women</strong>.</li>
					<li>Confirm by selecting <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
				</ol>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h3>Android</h3>
				<ol>
					<li>Open the site in Google Chrome.</li>
					<li>Open the browser menu and select <strong>Add to Home screen</strong> or <strong>Install app</strong>.</li>
					<li>Confirm by selecting <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
				</ol>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h3>iPhone</h3>
				<ol>
					<li>Open the site in Safari.</li>
					<li>Tap the <strong>Share</strong> button, then select <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong>.</li>
					<li>Tap <strong>Add</strong>.</li>
				</ol>
			</section>
		</div>
		<h2>Privacy</h2>
		<p>Favorites are stored only in your browser using local storage. The production site uses Azure Application Insights to collect anonymous page views, approximate visitor and session counts, performance data, browser errors, and favorite add or remove events. Favorite events include only the profile identifier and whether the action occurred on the catalog or profile page. We do not send names, email addresses, LinkedIn data, or your complete favorites list.</p>
		<h2>Sources and images</h2>
		<p>
			Content is adapted from <strong>Wikipedia</strong>, a free encyclopedia maintained by the Wikimedia Foundation.
			Available at: <a href="https://www.wikipedia.org/?utm_source=copilot.com" title="www.wikipedia.org" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">www.wikipedia.org</a>.
			Image provenance is credited separately to Wikipedia on each profile, with license terms governed by the original Wikipedia or Wikimedia Commons file page.
		</p>
		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>Questions, corrections, or suggestions? Connect with project creator <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ricklievano/" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">Rick Lievano on LinkedIn</a>.</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
